README.md

# SEO Flywheel (Skateboard) — bildaid module This module implements a minimal automated SEO flywheel: 1) Pull performance data (Google Search Console export/API) 2) Find near-win opportunities (positions ~8–20 with impressions) 3) Generate refresh plans + internal links 4) Publish updates to CMS (or create PRs) 5) Measure deltas and repeat 6) Expose observability via a dashboard page **Goal:** Start compounding from scratch with the least moving parts, then upgrade only when justified. ## What this module produces - A controller process (single-file friendly) that: - schedules SEO jobs - keeps state in SQLite - runs safely with dedupe + guardrails - A dashboard endpoint/page that shows: - pages processed - uplift metrics (clicks/impressions/avg position) - queue health / last run / errors ## Minimum dependencies (skateboard) - Google Search Console: file export OR API - CMS access: at least update a page or open a PR with changes - SQLite for state - LLM for structured refresh plan generation (can be stubbed) ## Quick start (agent-ready) 1) Copy `templates/env.example` → `.env` and fill values 2) Implement exactly ONE GSC adapter (export file is simplest) 3) Implement exactly ONE CMS adapter (stub/PR mode is simplest) 4) Add the dashboard page to your website 5) Set a daily cron job for the controller See: - `integration/website-integration.md` - `ops/runbook.md` - `dashboard/dashboard.spec.md` - `ops/upgrade-gates.md` 

module.spec.md

# Module Spec — SEO Flywheel (Skateboard) ## North Star A reliable, observable loop that repeatedly improves pages based on real search performance. ## Non-goals (for skateboard) - “Map the whole keyword universe” - Programmatic pages at scale - Automated link outreach - Complex data warehouse requirements ## Inputs - GSC performance rows: - page, query, impressions, clicks, avg_position, date_range - Website/CMS content: - HTML/MD body, title/meta, canonical URL ## Outputs - Updated pages OR PRs with updated content - Logged actions in SQLite - Dashboard metrics ## Core Jobs ### Job A: INGEST Bring GSC rows into SQLite from either: - export file (JSONL/CSV) OR - direct API OR - warehouse query ### Job B: SELECT_OPPORTUNITIES (Near-wins) Pick opportunities where: - impressions >= MIN_IMPRESSIONS - POS_MIN <= avg_position <= POS_MAX (default 8–20) - optional: CTR below expected for position - dedupe: one primary target query per page per run ### Job C: PLAN_REFRESH For each target page: - propose title/meta/H1 adjustments - propose sections to add based on related queries on that page - propose FAQ + optional schema - propose internal links to/from relevant pages ### Job D: APPLY_AND_PUBLISH Apply plan to content with guardrails: - max change size (diff threshold) - avoid repeating the same work (content hash) Publish: - direct update OR PR mode OR “todo list” mode ### Job E: MEASURE_DELTAS Weekly: - compare current vs baseline - calculate uplift - show in dashboard ## Guardrails - Dedupe by content hash and per-page cooldown window - Don’t publish if plan confidence low (missing required fields) - Keep changes incremental (append sections; avoid rewrites unless asked) - Human-in-the-loop toggle (PR or todo mode) ## Observability - /seo-flywheel dashboard page: - last run time, run duration - opportunities found, processed, published, skipped - top uplifts (clicks, impressions, avg position) - error log summary ## Config (.env) See `templates/env.example`. 

